General guidance for sending a scanned form that contains an SSN

1. Minimize what you send
- Only include the last 4 digits unless the recipient explicitly requires the full SSN.
- If the form itself (e.g., a government form) requires the full SSN, use a secure submission method (see below).

2. Prefer secure channels
- Use the recipient’s secure portal or an encrypted upload link whenever possible.
- If you must send via email, send a password‑protected (encrypted) PDF and share the password by phone or a different channel (SMS/call).

3. Proper redaction (do this instead of just covering text with a black box in an editor)
- Use a true redaction tool (Adobe Acrobat Pro “Redact” tool or another PDF redaction feature) so the removed text is irrecoverable.
- If you redact on an image, permanently flatten it (e.g., “Print to PDF” or export to a new flattened PDF) and then verify the original text can’t be selected/searched.
- Don’t rely on simple drawing/annotation layers or white rectangles — those can leave the underlying text intact.

4. Remove extras
- Strip metadata and hidden layers from the file before sending.
- Confirm there are no other documents or images attached that contain the full SSN.

5. Verify after redaction
- Open the saved/redacted file and try to select or search the SSN — if it can be found, the redaction wasn’t permanent.
- If possible, test-opening the file on a different device to ensure it’s actually encrypted or flattened.

6. If the recipient needs the full SSN
- Ask them to provide a secure upload link or instructions for an encrypted transmission.
- Alternatively: send a password‑protected PDF and give the password by phone; then delete any local copies you no longer need.

7. Recordkeeping and deletion
- Keep only the minimum needed copies, store encrypted at rest, and securely delete temporary files once the transfer is complete.

Quick sample message you could send to the recipient requesting a secure method
- “I’ve prepared the form with my SSN redacted to the last four digits. If you require the full SSN please provide a secure upload link or confirm I can send an encrypted PDF and I’ll call with the password.”

If you want, I can:
- Walk you step‑by‑step through redacting and creating a password‑protected PDF on your OS.
- Help draft the message requesting a secure upload link.

