1. Confirm whether the recipient actually needs the full SSN
   - Ask the recipient whether the last four digits are sufficient. Many organizations accept just the last 4; if they insist on the full SSN, ask for a secure upload portal or encrypted method.

2. Redact everything except the minimum required
   - If they only need the last four, redact the first five digits (the area and group numbers) so only the last 4 remain visible.
   - If they require the full SSN, request a secure method first (see item 4).

3. Use proper redaction (don’t just hide it visually)
   - Digital: use a true PDF redaction tool (Adobe Acrobat Pro “Redact”, or reputable redaction tools/websites). Redaction must remove the text from the file — not just place a black box over it — so the number can’t be recovered or extracted from the PDF or metadata.
