General rules
- Share the minimum needed. Most organizations only need the last 4 digits; only provide the full SSN if it’s explicitly required. Ask the requester why and whether a secure upload portal is available.
- If you must send a scanned copy, redact (remove) the unnecessary digits rather than just covering them visually. Proper redaction permanently removes the data (not just hides it).
- Always send scans through a secure channel (employer/government portal, encrypted email, or SFTP). Don’t send full SSNs in plain email or in file names.

How to redact safely (recommended approaches)
1. Best — use a PDF redaction tool that permanently deletes the text layer (Adobe Acrobat Pro):
   - Tools > Redact > Mark for Redaction (select the first five digits) > Apply Redactions > Save as a new file.
   - Also use “Remove Hidden Information”/“Sanitize” to clear metadata and thumbnails.

2. If you don’t have Acrobat — rasterize the page (so text becomes an image) then black out:
   - Print the PDF to a new PDF as an image (or export as PNG/JPEG).
   - Open the image in Preview (Mac) or Paint/GIMP (Windows), draw a solid black box over the first five digits, save, then export to PDF.
   - Confirm there’s no OCR/text layer left in the resulting PDF.

3. Mobile:
   - Use your phone’s markup on a saved image (but first convert to image so you remove any text layer). Don’t just draw over the PDF without removing the underlying layer.
   - Save and verify the image/PDF contains only the redacted text.

Remove metadata
- After redaction, remove metadata (author, creation dates). Acrobat has “Remove Hidden Information”; on macOS use File > Export and remove metadata where possible; on Windows use file Properties > Details > Remove Properties and Personal Information, or use a trusted PDF tool.

Protect the file in transit
- Use the recipient’s secure upload portal when available.
- If you must email, password-protect the PDF or put it in an encrypted zip. Send the password by a different channel (e.g., text or phone).
- Avoid putting SSN in the subject line or filename.

What to redact
- If only last 4 are needed: redact first five digits and label the visible as XXX-XX-1234 or simply show only the last four on the document.
- If full SSN is required: ask for a secure method to submit, then submit the full SSN via that secure channel only.

Extra tips
- Verify the requestor’s identity and retention/destruction policy before sending.
- Keep a copy of what you sent and to whom, and delete the unneeded file copies after confirmation the recipient received it.
- Never upload the full SSN to unknown third-party websites or free online converters.

If you tell me:
- Which last four is correct (7890 or 5678), and
- What device/app you’re using (Windows, Mac, iPhone/Android, Acrobat, Preview, etc.),

