Quick note before advice: you wrote "***-**-7890 (last four: 5678)". That looks inconsistent — please confirm whether the actual last four are 7890 or 5678.

General guidance
- Only share your full SSN when absolutely required. Ask the requester whether the last 4 digits will suffice — many organizations accept the last 4 instead of the full SSN.
- If the full SSN is not required, redact everything except the last four.
- If the full SSN is required, use secure transmission (see below).

How to redact a scanned document safely
1. Use a true redaction tool (best)
   - Adobe Acrobat Pro: Tools → Redact → Mark text for redaction → Apply Redactions → Save as a new file.
   - PDF editors with redaction features (PDF Expert, PDFpen, etc.) do the same: they remove the underlying text, not just hide it.
2. If you don’t have a redaction tool
   - Open the document, replace the SSN text with black boxes (edit the source file if possible), then export/print to PDF and “flatten” it (print-to-PDF) so layers are merged and text can’t be recovered.
   - Scanning a paper copy with the SSN obscured by a permanent black marker is a fallback — but it’s less reliable (marker may be translucent under some scans or recoverable by image processing). If you do this, test the resulting image/OCR to be sure the numbers are unrecoverable.
3. Always verify redaction
   - Try selecting text or running OCR on the redacted PDF to confirm the SSN cannot be copied or found.
4. Remove metadata
   - After redacting, remove document metadata and hidden layers (some PDF editors have “Remove metadata” or “Sanitize” options).
5. Encrypt the file for transmission
   - Password-protect the PDF (use a strong password) and send the password through a separate channel (e.g., SMS or phone call).
   - Prefer secure upload portals or an organization’s encrypted messaging system over regular email.

Transmission checklist
- Confirm recipient and why they need the SSN.
- Ask if last 4 digits will be sufficient.
- If full SSN is required, use a secure portal or password-protected/encrypted file.
- Keep a record of who you sent it to and when; minimize how long you retain copies.

If you want, I can:
- Draft a short message asking the recipient whether the last four are sufficient.
- Walk you step‑by‑step through redacting a specific file (tell me what software you have: Acrobat, Preview on Mac, Word, etc.).
- Double-check the instructions if you confirm which last-four is correct (7890 or 5678).

