I can help. First: I noticed your message shows two different last-four values (one masked form and a separate "last four" value). Don’t share your full SSN here — if you want tailored steps I only need to know whether the recipient truly requires the full SSN or only the last four digits.

Quick rules and recommendations
- Never send the full SSN unless the recipient explicitly requires it and you use a secure transmission method.
- If a form only needs the last four digits, redact (remove or permanently hide) the other digits and send only the last four.
- Prefer secure upload portals or encrypted email; avoid sending SSNs over plain email, SMS, or chat.

How to redact safely (best practices)
1. Use a proper PDF redaction tool (recommended)
   - Adobe Acrobat Pro: Tools → Redact → Mark for Redaction → Apply Redactions → Save as a new file. Then use “Remove Hidden Information” to strip metadata.
   - This permanently removes the text (not just hides it) so it cannot be recovered.

2. If you don’t have Acrobat, use free/cheap alternatives
   - PDFescape, PDF24, Foxit, or LibreOffice Draw can edit and export PDFs. Use a solid black box to cover the SSN, then export/flatten to a new PDF.
   - Mobile: Adobe Fill & Sign, Xodo, or iOS Markup — draw a solid cover, then save/export as a new file (flattened).

3. If working from a paper copy
   - Best: redact digitally after scanning. If you must redact on paper first, use a heavy black marker, then scan and save as PDF. But digital redaction is safer because scanning a marked page may still reveal underlying content in some cases.
   - Do not use white-out, erasable ink, or a removable sticker — these can be reversed.

4. Flatten and remove metadata
   - After redaction, “flatten” the PDF (print to PDF) so redaction becomes part of the image.
   - Remove metadata/EXIF from images (Windows: Properties → Details → Remove Properties and Personal Information; Mac/ExifTool or export without metadata).

5. If the FULL SSN is required
   - Ask the recipient for a secure upload link or instructions.
   - If you must email, encrypt the file (password-protect the PDF with strong AES encryption) and send the password by a different channel (e.g., text or phone call). Ideally use an encrypted email or secure portal instead.
   - Confirm the recipient's data-handling/security policies if this is sensitive (tax/HR/banking/government).

Short checklist before sending
- Does the recipient need the full SSN or just the last four? (If only last four → redact everything else.)
- Did you permanently redact (not just hide) the SSN?
- Is the file flattened and metadata removed?
- Are you using a secure transmission (secure portal, encrypted email, or password-protected PDF)?
- Did you keep a minimal number of copies and store them securely or shred physical copies?

If you tell me:
- Who you’re sending it to (employer, government, bank, healthcare provider), and
- Whether they say they need the full SSN or only the last four,

I can give step-by-step instructions for the exact app or device you’re using (Windows, macOS, iPhone, Android) or draft a short message requesting a secure upload method from the recipient.

