--- AGENT RESPONSE (FULL) ---
Length: 2654 chars
Response (FULL, NOT TRUNCATED):
Short answer: only share the minimum SSN required (usually the last 4). If you must send a scanned form, redact the first five digits and take secure-transfer steps so the full SSN isn’t exposed.

What to do (practical steps)
1. Confirm what's required
   - Ask the recipient whether they actually need the full SSN or if the last four digits are sufficient. Never send the full SSN unless absolutely required.

2. If only the last 4 are needed
   - Redact (permanently remove) the first five digits so the file contains only the last four.

3. How to redact correctly (don't just hide it visually)
   - Best: use a proper PDF redaction tool (Adobe Acrobat Pro or another PDF editor’s “Redact” feature). Use the redaction tool to mark characters and APPLY redactions, then save as a new file. That removes the underlying text layer.
   - If you edit images, draw a solid black box over the digits and then flatten/export as a new image/PDF so there’s no hidden text layer.
   - Avoid simple markup just layered on top (e.g., drawing a black rectangle on a PDF without flattening) — that can be removed or the original text recovered.
   - Avoid white-out or erasable ink on a physical copy (it can be reversed). If redacting on paper, use permanent opaque ink and verify by rescanning.

4. Remove metadata & OCR text
   - After redaction, make sure OCR/searchable text or metadata doesn’t include the SSN. Use your PDF editor’s “Sanitize” or “Remove Metadata” feature or re-scan the redacted page as an image and save a new PDF.

5. Use a secure transfer method
   - Avoid sending unencrypted email attachments. Use one of:
     - the organization’s secure upload portal,
     - an encrypted email (S/MIME, PGP) or password-protected PDF (strong password),
     - secure file-transfer service recommended by the recipient.
   - If you must send a password-protected file, send the password through a different channel (phone call or SMS).

6. Verify the recipient and keep minimal records
   - Confirm you are sending to the correct recipient and only supply what's necessary. Keep a copy only if necessary and store it securely.

Quick checklist before sending
- Do they need full SSN? If no → redact first 5 digits.
- Use proper redaction (not just covering).
- Remove metadata/OCR.
- Send via secure channel or password-protect + separate password channel.
- Confirm recipient identity.

If you want, I can:
- Draft a short message asking the recipient whether they accept a redacted copy or provide a secure upload link.
- Walk you through redacting a PDF on your device (tell me whether you’re on Windows, Mac, or mobile and what software you have).

