Short answer
- Only share the full SSN when the recipient explicitly requires it and they provide a secure channel. Otherwise, redact everything except the last 4 digits.
- If you must send a scan that includes the SSN, permanently redact the digits (don’t just hide them visually) and transfer the file over a secure method (secure portal, encrypted email, SFTP, or password-protected PDF with the password sent separately).

Detailed guidance and practical steps

1) Confirm necessity
- Ask the requester why they need the SSN and whether the last 4 digits will suffice.
- If they insist the full SSN is needed, ask for a secure upload link or an alternate secure method (encrypted email or portal).

2) Best redaction practices (what to do)
- Prefer permanent redaction tools (not just drawing a black box in an editor that leaves underlying text).
- After redaction, verify the SSN cannot be recovered by searching the PDF for those digits or selecting text.

3) How to redact safely (common methods)
- Adobe Acrobat Pro (recommended):
  - Tools → Redact → Mark for Redaction → select the SSN → Apply Redactions → Save As new file.
  - Then use “Sanitize Document” to remove hidden data/metadata.
- macOS Preview (workaround):
  - Use the Markup rectangle to cover the digits, then File → Export as PDF. This may not remove underlying text. To be safer: export the page as an image (File → Export → choose PNG/JPEG), open the image, black out the SSN, then print that image to PDF (File → Print → Save as PDF). Confirm you cannot select/search the text afterward.
- Free/Open-source tools:
  - Use a dedicated redaction tool (e.g., PDF Redact Tools) that permanently removes content, or an online redaction tool only if you trust and accept the service’s security/privacy terms.
- Physical paper:
  - Cover the SSN with opaque tape or use a solid label, then photocopy/scan the covered paper so the original digits are not captured. For the strictest assurance, black marker the SSN on the original, then make a new copy that you scan — but be sure marker ink doesn’t show through the paper.

4) After redaction — safety checks
- Open the redacted PDF and try to select or search for the SSN digits. If you can, the redaction is not permanent.
- Remove metadata: use a “sanitize” feature or clear document properties.
- Don’t include the SSN in the filename or email subject.

5) Transfer securely
- Use the recipient’s secure portal if available.
